{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Path"},{"type":"text","text":" with the edges it takes, paired with its length. Paths are told apart by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their edges, so parallel edges give distinct paths. Paths of equal length come in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unspecified order. The out-edges and their weights are copied when the sequence is made; each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"path after the first then costs up to one shortest-path search per vertex on the path before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. Taking a prefix, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"prefix(k)"},{"type":"text","text":", gives the k shortest simple paths."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each iterator starts over from the first path. Holds a copy of the graph, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShortestPathTree"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths0a6SimpleB0V","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ShortestSimplePaths.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestSimplePaths.swift#L326"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ShortestSimplePaths"}],"modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ShortestSimplePaths","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"ShortestSimplePaths","symbolKind":"struct"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestSimplePaths\/Iterator"],"anchor":"Structures","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestSimplePaths\/makeIterator()"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/S